    <description>The VLT spectrometer and imager for mid-infrared (VISIR) was developed by CEA/DAPNIA/SAP and NFRA/ASTRON and is situated at the Cassegrain focus of UT3 (Melipal). It offers high sensitivity, diffraction-limited imaging in three mid-infrared atmospheric windows: the M-band (5µm), the N-band (8-13µm), and the Q band (17-20µm). Additionally, it includes a long-slit spectrometer with spectral resolutions ranging from 150 to 30,000.</description>
